1
00:00:12,554 --> 00:00:13,680
How have you been?

2
00:00:17,809 --> 00:00:18,977
Can we talk?

3
00:00:21,021 --> 00:00:21,855
Sure.

4
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:23,732
We should.

5
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:27,902
But before that…

6
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:29,237
- Fucking…
- Wait!

7
00:00:29,904 --> 00:00:32,073
- Hear me out!
- You bastard!

8
00:00:38,913 --> 00:00:40,623
They're at it again. Fucking hell.

9
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:43,877
What the fuck are the police doing,
letting people like that walk free?

10
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,463
Hurry up and eat, you bitch!
Aren't you going to work?

11
00:00:46,963 --> 00:00:49,424
Always giving me shit. For fuck's sake.

12
00:01:00,268 --> 00:01:01,603
Come here, you bastard!

13
00:01:04,147 --> 00:01:05,273
Everyone out.

14
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:09,319
Get the fuck out, you bastards!

15
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:11,988
Wait.

16
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:14,032
Don't go.

17
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:18,745
It's gonna be a long night.

18
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:21,456
Luckily, I have plenty of time tonight.

19
00:01:21,998 --> 00:01:23,083
You fucking piece of shit.

20
00:01:26,586 --> 00:01:27,420
Fuck!

21
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:36,930
You're still alive?

22
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:38,890
Thought you came here with a death wish.

23
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:40,892
- Why aren't you dead yet?
- Your money.

24
00:01:42,185 --> 00:01:43,394
You want it back, right?

25
00:01:46,439 --> 00:01:49,359
Is my money still alive?

26
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:51,653
Find someone for me.

27
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:54,697
Then I'll give you your money back.

28
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:05,750
Look at this bastard.

29
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:08,586
Fine. Who should I find?

30
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:11,798
Me.

31
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,679
What the hell are you saying?

32
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:19,973
Please

33
00:02:20,473 --> 00:02:21,641
find me.

34
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:26,437
I lost myself.

35
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:31,025
You fucking bastard.

36
00:02:35,071 --> 00:02:36,030
Please…

37
00:02:36,114 --> 00:02:38,908
Please find me.

38
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:18,948
MOUSETRAP

39
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:21,576
I sent all the money we agreed on.

40
00:03:23,411 --> 00:03:25,038
We're done now, right?

41
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:26,873
Right, Moon-jae?

42
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:29,751
Hello?

43
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:32,253
Hello?

44
00:03:34,172 --> 00:03:36,883
<i>Stay sharp until it's all wrapped up.</i>

45
00:03:37,383 --> 00:03:39,469
<i>Just hang in there until then.</i>

46
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:41,971
Okay. Don't worry.

47
00:03:43,139 --> 00:03:45,141
Oh, but we…

48
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:58,279
So,

49
00:03:59,239 --> 00:04:01,908
you got cleaned out
by a guy who looks exactly like you?

50
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:03,952
Your house, money, everything?

51
00:04:06,287 --> 00:04:07,664
You expect me to believe that?

52
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:11,042
You bastard, if you were me,
would you just believe that?

53
00:04:11,125 --> 00:04:12,752
I can't believe it either.

54
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:15,880
But it's true.

55
00:04:17,173 --> 00:04:19,509
There's nothing left in my name.

56
00:04:20,009 --> 00:04:21,803
That bastard even changed my ID number.

57
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:25,139
Officially, I'm not Je Moon-jae anymore.

58
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:27,725
I'm just an empty shell.

59
00:04:29,435 --> 00:04:32,647
A person who doesn't exist, dead or alive.

60
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:37,026
I have to catch him.

61
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:40,655
The bastard who looks like me.

62
00:04:40,738 --> 00:04:45,076
You're the only one
who can prove I'm Je Moon-jae.

63
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:48,788
And only you can help me.

64
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:52,208
Why the fuck would I help you?
I should be killing you, you asshole.

65
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:55,086
You need to find your money.
And I need to find my name.

66
00:04:57,964 --> 00:04:59,716
<i>I have more than enough money.</i>

67
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:01,384
Money isn't the issue for me.

68
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:03,720
Okay? Life is.

69
00:05:04,345 --> 00:05:06,764
I've gotten tired of it, you see.

70
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:09,142
All you need to do is write.

71
00:05:09,225 --> 00:05:10,184
Give me the rights,

72
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:13,646
and I'll make it take off, film or TV.

73
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:15,273
- Okay?
- Okay.

74
00:05:20,069 --> 00:05:21,029
<i>If I'm lying, Noja,</i>

75
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:22,613
beat me to death.

76
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:24,282
Why do you keep calling me Noja?

77
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:26,951
Am I your friend or something,
you bastard?

78
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:30,038
You told me to use your name.

79
00:05:33,249 --> 00:05:34,417
Is this your place?

80
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:38,421
Here.

81
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:40,173
What's this?

82
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:42,800
I got one for you.
Go write something good.

83
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:44,260
I already have a laptop.

84
00:05:44,344 --> 00:05:47,764
Just use this one.
We're in the same boat now.

85
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:51,142
Thank you, sir.

86
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:52,518
For God's sake.

87
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:54,270
"Sir"? Are we thugs or what?

88
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:55,980
Just call me Noja.

89
00:05:56,981 --> 00:05:57,982
Okay, Noja.

90
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:02,820
Finding people?
Don't worry. I'm an expert.

91
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:07,283
But if you screw me over again,

92
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,453
you'll suffer a long, slow death.

93
00:06:10,536 --> 00:06:12,080
You won't die easily.

94
00:06:13,373 --> 00:06:16,667
I spent three fucking years
looking for this bastard.

95
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:19,337
Now I have to find another one
who looks exactly like him?

96
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:22,131
You gotta be fucking kidding me.

97
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:24,258
We must find someone else first.

98
00:06:25,843 --> 00:06:28,137
Fucking hell.

99
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:29,597
Who is it now?

100
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:32,392
My friend who had me skim money off you.

101
00:06:32,475 --> 00:06:34,310
It'll be faster to find him first.

102
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:35,895
They're in it together.

103
00:06:35,978 --> 00:06:37,647
Jesus, how…

104
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:41,234
How the fuck did I get mixed up
with this bastard?

105
00:06:48,408 --> 00:06:49,242
Listen carefully.

106
00:06:50,118 --> 00:06:52,328
You're my hostage now.

107
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:56,833
If I find my money, you live.
If I don't, you fucking die. Got it?

108
00:06:57,542 --> 00:07:00,169
Do everything you can to help me
if you want to live.

109
00:07:03,798 --> 00:07:05,341
- Okay.
- Damn it!

110
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:07,969
Goddamn it.

111
00:07:30,074 --> 00:07:31,993
Do you really have to go this far?

112
00:07:32,076 --> 00:07:34,287
How am I supposed to sleep like this?

113
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:40,668
Can't you at least loosen it a bit?

114
00:08:07,069 --> 00:08:08,905
PRIVATE DETECTIVE AGENCY

115
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:11,365
What?

116
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:13,284
He got caught already?

117
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:19,415
Huh?

118
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:27,507
Oh, he went there on his own.

119
00:08:31,427 --> 00:08:32,887
This is getting interesting.

120
00:08:43,189 --> 00:08:45,149
Excuse me?

121
00:08:48,486 --> 00:08:51,072
We're not open yet. Lunch starts at noon.

122
00:08:51,155 --> 00:08:53,449
Oh, I'm not here to eat.

123
00:08:54,158 --> 00:08:55,826
You know Mr. Kim Yeong-geun, right?

124
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:58,913
Could you tell me where he is?

125
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:02,750
Sir?

126
00:09:06,003 --> 00:09:07,713
Who even is that?

127
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:09,215
Huh?

128
00:09:10,091 --> 00:09:11,717
I heard you used to work together.

129
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:14,178
Oh, come on.

130
00:09:14,679 --> 00:09:17,223
Don't be like that.
If you know, just tell me.

131
00:09:17,306 --> 00:09:19,016
Where are you from?

132
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,935
I'm with the police.

133
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:30,903
Jeez, don't bother the guy.
He's clean now.

134
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:32,238
God.

135
00:09:32,321 --> 00:09:34,574
What, you think other people
don't live clean?

136
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:38,786
Just tell me where your "clean" guy is.

137
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:43,749
It's nothing serious.
It'll just take a minute.

138
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:45,501
I just need to see him for a moment.

139
00:09:48,045 --> 00:09:49,338
What's this about?

140
00:09:50,047 --> 00:09:52,675
I came because he didn't pay a fine.

141
00:09:53,175 --> 00:09:54,135
A fine?

142
00:09:54,218 --> 00:09:56,887
A summary summons. Why won't he take it?

143
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,723
The fine's not even 200,000 won.

144
00:09:58,806 --> 00:10:02,310
If he keeps this up, his assets
could get seized over a 200,000-won fine.

145
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:04,186
I'm busy as hell already.

146
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:09,859
Have a good one!

147
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:19,493
PRIVATE DETECTIVE AGENCY

148
00:10:27,752 --> 00:10:31,339
I'd be retired by now
if I'd put that money into real estate.

149
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:36,135
That no-good bastard.

150
00:10:36,719 --> 00:10:39,221
How did I end up
getting mixed up with him?

151
00:10:41,223 --> 00:10:44,268
To become a new man…
I was crazy to trust him.

152
00:10:44,352 --> 00:10:46,646
If a thug becomes a businessman,

153
00:10:47,146 --> 00:10:48,981
does that make him a new man?

154
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:51,776
That's basically identity fraud.

155
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:55,613
Don't push it.

156
00:10:55,696 --> 00:10:56,530
Okay?

157
00:10:56,614 --> 00:11:00,409
Because of you, I never became a new man.
I'm still the same old me, you bastard.

158
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:02,662
I'm a dangerous man. You hear me?

159
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:05,122
What is he blabbering about?

160
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:08,042
All right. Let's go.

161
00:11:09,293 --> 00:11:12,338
To catch the bastard who stole
from the bastard who stole from me.

162
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:28,979
His address might be registered with
the accountants' association or something.

163
00:11:29,563 --> 00:11:32,274
For lawyers and accountants,
associations are important.

164
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:37,905
Are you listening?

165
00:11:38,906 --> 00:11:40,199
Yeah. I hear you!

166
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:43,703
But I've got a plan too, so just zip it.

167
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:46,330
Where are we going?

168
00:11:48,416 --> 00:11:50,751
We're on our way
to meet the blog owner you found.

169
00:11:51,419 --> 00:11:55,297
The one who posted the reunion photos.
That's how you got to the reunion, right?

170
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:56,966
You know where he is?

171
00:11:57,049 --> 00:12:01,971
Know what's wrong with kids these days?
They put their personal info everywhere.

172
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:05,391
Blog, Instagram.
His personal info is everywhere.

173
00:12:05,474 --> 00:12:07,393
These days, if you hack someone's phone,

174
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:10,563
you can clean them out in an instant.

175
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:13,399
Don't ever post stuff online.

176
00:12:15,568 --> 00:12:18,529
Criminals and would-be criminals
shouldn't do that.

177
00:12:18,612 --> 00:12:19,530
Got it?

178
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:23,451
BOARD-CERTIFIED PLASTIC SURGEON, MD

179
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:26,912
Wow, you must be pretty good with a knife.

180
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:30,291
You're basically creating faces
from scratch, huh?

181
00:12:30,374 --> 00:12:32,418
This is straight-up identity fraud.

182
00:12:32,501 --> 00:12:36,881
Isn't that illegal,
changing someone's face like that?

183
00:12:36,964 --> 00:12:38,048
- Damn it.
- Huh?

184
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:40,134
Kyeong-tae. You really don't remember me?

185
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:43,012
It's me, Moon-jae. Je Moon-jae.
And you're…

186
00:12:43,929 --> 00:12:45,973
You're Jeon Kyeong-tae.
Your last name, Jeon.

187
00:12:46,056 --> 00:12:47,475
You really don't remember me?

188
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:49,894
What do you two think you're doing?
Seriously?

189
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:51,937
Then call the police.

190
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:55,357
What, you think I won't call the police?

191
00:12:57,359 --> 00:12:58,486
What are you trying to--

192
00:13:00,362 --> 00:13:02,364
How about some plastic surgery, Doc?

193
00:13:08,496 --> 00:13:09,663
SON SOO-HYUN

194
00:13:11,290 --> 00:13:15,211
<i>The number you've dialed does not exist.</i>
<i>Please check and try again.</i>

195
00:13:15,294 --> 00:13:17,546
That bastard totally went off the grid.

196
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:20,007
This guy's not involved.

197
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:26,597
<i>You can't go to crowded places.</i>

198
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:29,767
You can't go to open spaces,
and you don't like tight spaces either.

199
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:32,937
You've got so many fucking issues.

200
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:35,147
Burgers taste best at the joint.

201
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:40,444
Sometimes you're fine,
sometimes you're not.

202
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:44,448
It's all because of your guilt, punk.

203
00:13:44,532 --> 00:13:46,325
The guilt of running off with my money!

204
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:56,794
I need my meds.

205
00:13:57,962 --> 00:14:01,507
I'm anxious. I never know
when the symptoms will flare up.

206
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:03,467
You said you need a prescription.

207
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:06,846
Why didn't you get that doctor
to write you one, you dumbass?

208
00:14:10,724 --> 00:14:13,185
Soo-hyun always got them for me. Damn it.

209
00:14:24,697 --> 00:14:27,283
Why are you looking at me?
Am I your errand boy, punk?

210
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,410
Did somebody say that?

211
00:14:30,703 --> 00:14:32,162
Aren't we on the same team?

212
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:34,123
We're in the same boat!

213
00:14:34,206 --> 00:14:36,917
You no-good bastard. Seriously.

214
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:43,257
Move aside.

215
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:47,887
Just take these and get by for now.

216
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:50,723
What's this?

217
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:54,184
One's a painkiller.
I don't know what the other one is.

218
00:14:56,478 --> 00:14:59,940
I can't just take any meds.

219
00:15:00,858 --> 00:15:03,485
You don't know the story
of Wonhyo and the skull water?

220
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:05,487
It's all about how you take it, punk!

221
00:15:11,035 --> 00:15:13,996
Who's that bastard impersonating me?

222
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:20,669
Soo-hyun brought him to the reunion
about a year ago.

223
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:22,630
At first, we didn't recognize him,

224
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:25,174
but then he looked like the guy
in the graduation pic.

225
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:27,301
So we thought he was Moon-jae.

226
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:30,429
See? They're in this together.

227
00:15:30,512 --> 00:15:32,640
But this doesn't make any sense.

228
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,726
I've had drinks with Moon-jae
so many times recently.

229
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:38,896
Turns out, he's a famous writer.

230
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:42,608
But

231
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:46,403
you don't even remember
what happened on our school trip.

232
00:15:46,904 --> 00:15:48,864
That's not something you forget!

233
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:50,991
Moon-jae remembered it clearly.

234
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:54,787
You keep going on about some school trip.
What about it?

235
00:15:54,870 --> 00:15:57,456
What happened? Let's hear it. What is it?

236
00:15:58,791 --> 00:16:00,793
There was a fire.

237
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:05,297
All the students had to evacuate.
It was a total mess.

238
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:10,177
And you don't remember that?

239
00:16:11,929 --> 00:16:13,263
Does that make sense?

240
00:16:28,195 --> 00:16:29,863
You are Je Moon-jae, right?

241
00:16:34,827 --> 00:16:37,121
And he got plastic surgery
just for the money?

242
00:16:38,330 --> 00:16:40,249
Why? He could've just taken it all.

243
00:16:40,332 --> 00:16:42,835
You said it was in that bastard's account.

244
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:47,589
Because it was Je Moon-jae's money.

245
00:16:48,298 --> 00:16:50,926
And I'm not Je Moon-jae anymore.

246
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:56,098
Even if you go to the police,
you'd be a Je Moon-jae impersonator?

247
00:16:56,181 --> 00:16:57,391
I guess so.

248
00:16:58,308 --> 00:17:03,063
And he lured me with a card in your name
so I could find you, huh?

249
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:05,607
Because I'd kill you if I caught you.

250
00:17:05,691 --> 00:17:07,276
I'd be doing his dirty work.

251
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:09,987
Then why did he warn me to run?

252
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:12,197
Why not just let you kill me?

253
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:14,575
Maybe the job's not done yet.

254
00:17:14,658 --> 00:17:17,578
Maybe he hasn't moved all the money.

255
00:17:21,081 --> 00:17:22,166
That could be it.

256
00:17:26,795 --> 00:17:28,589
That's an interesting bastard.

257
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:34,678
You mean "bastards."

258
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:38,057
You little shit.

259
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,224
Where are we going now?

260
00:17:46,482 --> 00:17:47,900
Hey, where are we going?

261
00:17:59,995 --> 00:18:03,165
I told you. This is a waste of time.
I've been here before.

262
00:18:03,248 --> 00:18:05,709
You only see what you know.

263
00:18:07,836 --> 00:18:08,670
I mean…

264
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:12,925
You coming?

265
00:18:31,652 --> 00:18:32,486
It's just…

266
00:18:34,321 --> 00:18:35,531
Elevators are a bit…

267
00:18:36,573 --> 00:18:38,242
What a load of bullshit.

268
00:18:41,328 --> 00:18:43,080
Must be great exercise.

269
00:18:56,009 --> 00:18:57,719
If you scratch someone's car,

270
00:18:57,803 --> 00:19:00,347
any civilized person
would leave their number.

271
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:03,725
You accountants are all educated, right?
Am I wrong?

272
00:19:04,226 --> 00:19:05,853
What's this country coming to?

273
00:19:05,936 --> 00:19:06,812
Just a moment.

274
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:09,815
He doesn't work here anymore.
I'll check the parking log to…

275
00:19:09,898 --> 00:19:13,318
Here it is. A white BMW. Is that correct?

276
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:14,903
- Yes, white.
- Okay.

277
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:18,157
- What's that bastard's plate number?
- The plate number is…

278
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:23,203
Hey, we're done here. See you downstairs.

279
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:39,052
No, that's not it.

280
00:19:41,054 --> 00:19:43,348
Yeah, white. 5340.

281
00:19:43,432 --> 00:19:45,475
Got it. Find out fast!

282
00:19:50,606 --> 00:19:51,732
Did you find him?

283
00:19:55,569 --> 00:19:58,906
ENTER AMOUNT
2,000,000 WON

284
00:19:58,989 --> 00:19:59,865
Okay.

285
00:20:00,574 --> 00:20:01,992
I asked if you found it.

286
00:20:02,075 --> 00:20:04,786
Fuck, you've gotta wait.

287
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:05,913
For who?

288
00:20:05,996 --> 00:20:08,248
None of your business.
It's a trade secret.

289
00:20:23,138 --> 00:20:24,431
WHITE BMW 5340
1,500,000 WON REWARD

290
00:20:29,186 --> 00:20:30,062
WHITE BMW 5340 WANTED

291
00:20:51,416 --> 00:20:52,417
WHITE BMW 5340 WANTED

292
00:21:31,957 --> 00:21:33,625
Money exchange, huh?

293
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:37,462
Shit, I screwed up.

294
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:40,841
I guess you can smoke in here.

295
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:43,218
Oh, that's great.

296
00:21:47,347 --> 00:21:48,890
Oh, you can't?

297
00:21:53,186 --> 00:21:54,521
What is this place?

298
00:21:55,605 --> 00:21:57,607
What do you mean? It's just an office.

299
00:21:57,691 --> 00:21:58,817
Why?

300
00:21:58,900 --> 00:21:59,818
Oh, come on.

301
00:21:59,901 --> 00:22:02,946
What kind of office has no computers?

302
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:04,406
Hi.

303
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:06,241
- Hey, babe.
- Yeah.

304
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:07,409
Hello.

305
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:08,368
Look.

306
00:22:08,452 --> 00:22:11,246
I'm not interested
in your illegal escort stuff, okay?

307
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:13,415
Are you close with the guys upstairs?

308
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:16,752
- Why?
- I'm just interested.

309
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:18,462
I don't wanna get involved.

310
00:22:18,545 --> 00:22:19,796
And you won't be.

311
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:22,466
Don't worry.
My life is already complicated enough.

312
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:26,428
I'm not lying.

313
00:22:28,180 --> 00:22:30,015
I hear he finds people for a living.

314
00:22:30,515 --> 00:22:32,351
Well, it's a private detective agency.

315
00:22:32,976 --> 00:22:33,810
He's different.

316
00:22:34,311 --> 00:22:36,104
He can even find unidentified people.

317
00:22:36,188 --> 00:22:39,983
Even if you hide from your debts,
he'll track you down in no time.

318
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:43,111
You know those guys
who run online gambling sites?

319
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:45,364
- Yeah.
- They come around a lot.

320
00:22:46,323 --> 00:22:48,867
They really went after someone yesterday.

321
00:22:48,950 --> 00:22:51,995
But if they beat up people like that,

322
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:53,288
wouldn't they die?

323
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:56,083
They probably would.

324
00:22:58,043 --> 00:22:59,378
Anyway,

325
00:22:59,878 --> 00:23:02,047
don't let him know I said this.

326
00:23:02,714 --> 00:23:04,591
He looks scary as hell.

327
00:23:04,674 --> 00:23:07,594
I get scared
every time I see him in the hallway.

328
00:23:09,346 --> 00:23:12,140
It must've been hard for you. Here.

329
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:14,351
PARK SUN-YONG

330
00:23:15,310 --> 00:23:17,104
Let's keep in touch, okay?

331
00:23:18,605 --> 00:23:21,400
Fuck. You said I wouldn't be involved.

332
00:23:21,483 --> 00:23:23,276
I'm just interested.

333
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:26,363
Take care.

334
00:23:29,074 --> 00:23:30,158
The fuck?

335
00:23:45,257 --> 00:23:50,470
EVERYTHING WILL BE FINE, SO DON'T WORRY
IT'S ALMOST OVER, OKAY?

336
00:23:57,477 --> 00:23:58,937
It's almost over.

337
00:23:59,604 --> 00:24:01,523
It's almost over.

338
00:24:12,784 --> 00:24:13,994
5340?

339
00:24:15,871 --> 00:24:18,915
SEOUL DELIVERY RIDERS ASSOCIATION
WHITE BMW 5340 WANTED

340
00:24:32,554 --> 00:24:35,557
The Heart Sutra
has nothing to do with Noja.

341
00:24:36,808 --> 00:24:39,519
Just listen and be grateful, damn it.

342
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:41,897
It's why you're still alive.

343
00:24:44,441 --> 00:24:46,776
But why does this bastard look familiar?

344
00:24:47,277 --> 00:24:49,404
Maybe it's because he looks so plain?

345
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:52,866
I'm surprised
he's still active on social media.

346
00:24:52,949 --> 00:24:54,618
It's private now.

347
00:24:54,701 --> 00:24:57,954
I downloaded this early this morning.

348
00:24:58,955 --> 00:25:00,540
Early this morning?

349
00:25:01,666 --> 00:25:02,584
You're diligent.

350
00:25:02,667 --> 00:25:05,587
You gotta be more diligent
than the ones who ran off.

351
00:25:05,670 --> 00:25:08,882
Nothing in life is easy. Okay?

352
00:25:10,217 --> 00:25:13,345
Everything's tough and exhausting.
That's life.

353
00:25:14,304 --> 00:25:16,056
So you were lazy chasing me, huh?

354
00:25:16,932 --> 00:25:19,017
You hid out for three years.

355
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:21,728
How was I supposed to catch you,
you little shit?

356
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:23,230
Damn it.

357
00:25:27,442 --> 00:25:28,276
Hello?

358
00:25:29,986 --> 00:25:31,071
Yeah. Okay.

359
00:25:31,571 --> 00:25:33,240
Send me the address.

360
00:25:35,242 --> 00:25:37,160
What? They already found him?

361
00:25:39,496 --> 00:25:40,830
But he's still in Seoul.

362
00:25:41,414 --> 00:25:42,874
Why didn't he run?

363
00:25:43,458 --> 00:25:45,335
If I were him, I'd have run by now.

364
00:25:45,418 --> 00:25:47,504
You were right. He's still got loose ends.

365
00:26:18,451 --> 00:26:19,452
Who are you?

366
00:26:20,078 --> 00:26:21,329
You know me?

367
00:26:24,165 --> 00:26:25,041
What is it?

368
00:26:36,678 --> 00:26:39,889
RUN AWAY. RIGHT NOW.

369
00:27:15,258 --> 00:27:16,384
Goddamn it.

370
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:18,178
Just stay here, punk!

371
00:27:19,679 --> 00:27:20,972
Shit.

372
00:27:33,360 --> 00:27:34,361
Damn it.

373
00:27:51,086 --> 00:27:52,671
Fuck!

374
00:28:03,348 --> 00:28:04,349
Damn it.

375
00:28:11,272 --> 00:28:12,691
Hey, punk. You good?

376
00:28:15,235 --> 00:28:16,986
God, you no-good bastard. Seriously.

377
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:24,536
You said that bastard
had a guy tailing me, right?

378
00:28:24,619 --> 00:28:25,578
Yeah.

379
00:28:25,662 --> 00:28:28,123
He was tailing me a couple of days ago.
I ran into him.

380
00:28:28,206 --> 00:28:30,250
I should've roughed that bastard up more.

381
00:28:30,333 --> 00:28:33,169
How was I supposed to know
that bastard was him?

382
00:28:33,253 --> 00:28:34,879
He even ditched his car.

383
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:36,881
He must've been in a hurry.

384
00:28:36,965 --> 00:28:38,425
So we wait here for him?

385
00:28:40,802 --> 00:28:42,178
What if he doesn't come back?

386
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:53,189
But it's strange.

387
00:28:53,690 --> 00:28:55,400
The timing is just too perfect.

388
00:28:55,483 --> 00:29:01,030
Huh? How did he stay one step ahead of us?

389
00:29:17,130 --> 00:29:18,506
There's not much there.

390
00:29:19,382 --> 00:29:21,259
There's a lot here!

391
00:29:22,051 --> 00:29:23,511
Look at the dates, you punk!

392
00:29:23,595 --> 00:29:25,346
These are all from a few days ago!

393
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:27,599
He's had his dashcam off for days.

394
00:29:27,682 --> 00:29:31,269
He knew someone would search the car
if things went south.

395
00:29:37,108 --> 00:29:38,818
What do we do now?

396
00:29:39,861 --> 00:29:41,237
You've got a plan B, right?

397
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:43,448
You said you're an expert
at finding people.

398
00:29:47,327 --> 00:29:49,120
- That'll be 70,000 won.
- Right.

399
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:53,374
That'll be 2,000,000 today.

400
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:56,336
Gas, food, my time, and all that.

401
00:29:56,419 --> 00:29:58,880
You'll be charged for all this.
You know that, right?

402
00:29:58,963 --> 00:30:02,675
If a client hires a private detective,
they should pay up.

403
00:30:07,597 --> 00:30:09,390
Client? You said I'm your hostage.

404
00:30:09,891 --> 00:30:10,975
You're both.

405
00:30:14,646 --> 00:30:15,480
Where to?

406
00:30:15,563 --> 00:30:17,148
What's it to you?

407
00:30:17,232 --> 00:30:21,402
I don't care if I'm a hostage or a client.
Just tell me where we're going!

408
00:30:23,738 --> 00:30:26,324
We're going with plan B, you punk.
Happy now?

409
00:30:39,170 --> 00:30:44,008
Those who run can hide themselves,
but they can't hide their families.

410
00:30:44,092 --> 00:30:45,093
Why?

411
00:30:45,176 --> 00:30:48,012
Even within a family,
each person has their own life.

412
00:30:49,806 --> 00:30:52,141
How did you know Soo-hyun's kid goes here?

413
00:30:52,225 --> 00:30:53,518
Instagram.

414
00:30:54,102 --> 00:30:55,854
That damn Instagram.

415
00:30:57,063 --> 00:30:59,190
- Where to?
- Aren't we here for his address?

416
00:30:59,274 --> 00:31:02,026
You think they'll just tell you?
They don't know you.

417
00:31:02,110 --> 00:31:04,779
You really don't know
how the world works, do you?

418
00:31:04,863 --> 00:31:05,697
Close the door!

419
00:31:06,739 --> 00:31:07,574
Open that.

420
00:31:09,409 --> 00:31:10,869
Give me one. Hurry.

421
00:31:17,125 --> 00:31:19,627
What's all this?

422
00:31:19,711 --> 00:31:21,004
This one's way too far.

423
00:31:21,087 --> 00:31:23,673
Give me a closer one. One in Seoul.

424
00:31:23,756 --> 00:31:25,550
Seoul. Right.

425
00:31:27,844 --> 00:31:29,053
SEOUL MAPO POLICE STATION

426
00:31:30,763 --> 00:31:31,931
Stay here.

427
00:31:32,932 --> 00:31:33,892
Why?

428
00:31:33,975 --> 00:31:36,686
Just stay here, punk!
Ever seen a detective in sweats?

429
00:31:44,485 --> 00:31:48,114
Da-eun hasn't been in for a few days.

430
00:31:48,197 --> 00:31:51,576
So I called her mother,
and she said Da-eun's taking a break.

431
00:31:51,659 --> 00:31:53,536
Seems like it's a family matter.

432
00:31:54,370 --> 00:31:56,080
What kind of family matter?

433
00:31:56,164 --> 00:31:57,081
I'm not sure.

434
00:31:57,165 --> 00:31:59,918
She just said
Da-eun's taking a break for a while.

435
00:32:02,211 --> 00:32:05,173
I guess I'll have to go to this address
and ask myself.

436
00:32:05,757 --> 00:32:07,675
What's this about?

437
00:32:07,759 --> 00:32:10,511
Da-eun's parents aren't the kind
to commit a crime.

438
00:32:12,055 --> 00:32:15,016
It's always the ones you least suspect
who do it.

439
00:32:15,516 --> 00:32:17,435
All right. Thank you for your cooperation.

440
00:32:19,228 --> 00:32:20,313
Crap.

441
00:32:24,984 --> 00:32:26,235
We're with the police.

442
00:32:26,986 --> 00:32:29,530
Well. We're with the police.

443
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:32,116
What's wrong with him?

444
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:35,620
- What's going on?
- What?

445
00:32:35,703 --> 00:32:36,996
Why are the police here?

446
00:32:37,080 --> 00:32:38,456
What? Hey!

447
00:32:38,539 --> 00:32:39,582
Slow down!

448
00:32:40,959 --> 00:32:42,669
What's wrong? Someone's there!

449
00:32:43,544 --> 00:32:45,672
What the hell is going on here?

450
00:32:51,386 --> 00:32:53,763
- Hey, did you see something?
- No.

451
00:32:53,846 --> 00:32:55,431
Jeez.

452
00:32:55,515 --> 00:32:56,849
Move, damn it.

453
00:32:58,267 --> 00:32:59,477
Goddamn it.

454
00:33:02,438 --> 00:33:03,356
It's so quiet.

455
00:33:03,982 --> 00:33:06,526
The cops even went to the daycare.
No way they are home.

456
00:33:09,862 --> 00:33:11,030
Cops! Get down!

457
00:33:11,531 --> 00:33:14,200
- Cops! Get the hell down.
- Cops?

458
00:33:16,703 --> 00:33:17,578
They're gone.

459
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:22,500
I didn't even report him.
Why did the police come for Soo-hyun?

460
00:33:23,334 --> 00:33:24,168
Yeah.

461
00:33:24,752 --> 00:33:26,295
What the hell has he been up to?

462
00:33:26,379 --> 00:33:29,298
You should've picked better friends,
you dumbass!

463
00:33:31,509 --> 00:33:32,969
Could be the car you smashed.

464
00:33:33,052 --> 00:33:35,680
Why would they go after his daughter
over that? You idiot!

465
00:33:38,641 --> 00:33:40,143
For fuck's sake.

466
00:33:41,644 --> 00:33:43,604
We need to reach him before the police do.

467
00:33:45,106 --> 00:33:47,608
Otherwise, fuck,
the money goes to the government.

468
00:33:52,488 --> 00:33:54,365
Don't worry. It'll be fine.

469
00:33:55,074 --> 00:33:56,743
Once everything's done,

470
00:33:57,243 --> 00:33:58,953
why don't we take a trip?

471
00:33:59,746 --> 00:34:01,748
You said you wanted to take a break.

472
00:34:02,248 --> 00:34:04,625
And we should let Da-eun see the world

473
00:34:05,126 --> 00:34:07,420
before she starts school.

474
00:34:13,885 --> 00:34:14,886
The police?

475
00:34:20,099 --> 00:34:22,435
I told you we just have to be patient
a bit longer.

476
00:34:22,518 --> 00:34:25,646
We were almost there.
Why couldn't you wait a few more days?!

477
00:34:25,730 --> 00:34:26,898
Why? Damn it!

478
00:34:38,409 --> 00:34:39,452
Shit.

479
00:34:53,257 --> 00:34:54,467
All day,

480
00:34:55,718 --> 00:34:59,514
all we had was a burger.

481
00:35:01,265 --> 00:35:02,558
I'm kinda hungry.

482
00:35:08,856 --> 00:35:10,525
Come on. Let's eat something.

483
00:35:14,278 --> 00:35:15,113
Are you buying?

484
00:35:15,863 --> 00:35:18,825
I've got no money.
Soo-hyun even blocked mobile payments.

485
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:20,785
How did he get his hands on your phone?

486
00:35:21,577 --> 00:35:23,162
He bought me this phone.

487
00:35:23,246 --> 00:35:25,081
That was a stupid question.

488
00:35:30,753 --> 00:35:31,587
Give it to me.

489
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:33,381
Give it!

490
00:35:34,590 --> 00:35:36,592
Huh? Hey! Why?

491
00:35:37,844 --> 00:35:39,470
No wonder his timing was perfect.

492
00:35:39,554 --> 00:35:42,098
He planted something on your phone,
you dumbass!

493
00:35:42,598 --> 00:35:43,975
He knew we were onto him!

494
00:35:44,058 --> 00:35:46,310
God, you stupid dumbass.

495
00:35:46,394 --> 00:35:47,937
Seriously! Goddamn it!

496
00:35:50,898 --> 00:35:52,567
Damn it.

497
00:35:55,403 --> 00:35:56,654
Still, you should've--

498
00:35:58,906 --> 00:36:00,158
What is it?

499
00:36:01,492 --> 00:36:03,202
Hey, go pick it up.

500
00:36:08,833 --> 00:36:09,917
It's over there.

501
00:36:20,469 --> 00:36:21,804
That fucking scared me.

502
00:36:21,888 --> 00:36:24,849
Why the hell does he keep calling me?
It's so annoying.

503
00:36:24,932 --> 00:36:25,850
Yes, sir.

504
00:36:25,933 --> 00:36:26,767
<i>Where are you?</i>

505
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:29,061
You told me to follow up on the tip.

506
00:36:29,562 --> 00:36:31,105
<i>You said it was a prank.</i>

507
00:36:31,856 --> 00:36:33,107
Yes, I did.

508
00:36:33,191 --> 00:36:35,359
<i>But something's bothering me.</i>

509
00:36:35,443 --> 00:36:36,277
You slacking off?

510
00:36:37,445 --> 00:36:39,572
What the fuck do you mean? Seriously.

511
00:36:41,657 --> 00:36:43,075
Don't we have work to do?

512
00:36:43,159 --> 00:36:46,329
<i>Everyone's working their asses off,</i>
<i>and you haven't shown up all day!</i>

513
00:36:46,412 --> 00:36:47,747
- I mean--
- <i>Hey.</i>

514
00:36:47,830 --> 00:36:49,749
Just file the report as is and wrap it up.

515
00:36:49,832 --> 00:36:52,710
But I should at least meet that thug.

516
00:36:52,793 --> 00:36:55,504
How the fuck am I supposed
to write this report or whatever?

517
00:36:55,588 --> 00:36:57,673
<i>Then did you at least find the bastard?</i>

518
00:36:58,299 --> 00:36:59,884
ESCORT LADY
HE JUST CAME IN

519
00:37:01,594 --> 00:37:03,512
I found him. Yes. I just fucking did!

520
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:04,430
<i>I just found him!</i>

521
00:37:04,513 --> 00:37:07,391
I'll file the report and close it out.
This is fucking bullshit.

522
00:37:08,976 --> 00:37:09,810
Huh?

523
00:37:21,072 --> 00:37:22,490
Just eat it already.

524
00:37:29,997 --> 00:37:31,123
Elders first.

525
00:37:31,207 --> 00:37:32,208
You bastard.

526
00:37:40,591 --> 00:37:41,759
Hey, hurry up and eat.

527
00:37:41,842 --> 00:37:42,969
We have to head out.

528
00:37:44,387 --> 00:37:45,388
We're going out again?

529
00:37:45,471 --> 00:37:47,223
- Where to?
- Somewhere.

530
00:37:48,975 --> 00:37:51,435
From now on,
don't ever tell me where we're going.

531
00:37:51,519 --> 00:37:52,979
Never ever tell me.

532
00:37:53,062 --> 00:37:54,522
If you do, I'll just--

533
00:37:54,605 --> 00:37:55,606
Fishing.

534
00:37:58,776 --> 00:37:59,777
Eat up.

535
00:38:02,405 --> 00:38:03,364
I'm done.

536
00:38:13,082 --> 00:38:15,001
Did you get rid of the one at the morgue?

537
00:38:16,544 --> 00:38:17,378
No, not yet.

538
00:38:19,797 --> 00:38:21,215
Hurry up and burn it.

539
00:38:22,925 --> 00:38:23,759
Yes, sir.

540
00:38:34,979 --> 00:38:35,938
PRIVATE DETECTIVE AGENCY

541
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:37,857
She said he was here. Damn it.

542
00:38:37,940 --> 00:38:40,067
The light's off. That lady…

543
00:38:57,918 --> 00:38:59,503
Who the hell is that?

544
00:39:00,379 --> 00:39:03,007
It's that bastard from yesterday.

545
00:39:03,090 --> 00:39:04,842
The one Noja beat the crap out of.

546
00:39:06,427 --> 00:39:08,179
So many new faces.

547
00:39:08,679 --> 00:39:10,139
That means things are fucked.

548
00:39:13,893 --> 00:39:15,394
Don't know him, huh?

549
00:39:15,478 --> 00:39:17,521
They were tearing into each other,

550
00:39:17,605 --> 00:39:19,106
and now they're friends?

551
00:39:19,190 --> 00:39:22,526
These bastards are just unbelievable.

552
00:39:47,927 --> 00:39:49,595
But how do you know he'll come?

553
00:39:49,678 --> 00:39:53,557
That bastard's very interested in you.
What you're doing and where you're going.

554
00:39:54,600 --> 00:39:57,770
He's tracking you all day on his phone.

555
00:39:59,647 --> 00:40:01,107
He's going to come check.

556
00:40:01,190 --> 00:40:02,274
Your dead body.

557
00:40:13,077 --> 00:40:16,372
GWANGNAM RESERVOIR

558
00:40:33,639 --> 00:40:34,890
Give me a tissue.

559
00:40:37,685 --> 00:40:39,478
Don't get too close, man.

560
00:40:39,562 --> 00:40:40,396
Yes, sir.

561
00:41:01,333 --> 00:41:02,626
This might take a while,

562
00:41:03,419 --> 00:41:05,212
so lie down and get comfortable.

563
00:41:11,051 --> 00:41:12,887
It's a good place to bury a body.

564
00:41:13,387 --> 00:41:15,973
You're dangerous, huh?
Must've buried a lot of bodies.

565
00:41:23,314 --> 00:41:24,732
Would they even care?

566
00:41:24,815 --> 00:41:27,359
Wouldn't it be better for them if I died?

567
00:41:27,443 --> 00:41:30,279
If their goal was to kill you,
you'd be dead already.

568
00:41:31,363 --> 00:41:32,907
Since you can't die yet,

569
00:41:32,990 --> 00:41:34,950
they'll come here to check on you.

570
00:41:35,034 --> 00:41:36,869
That's the point of this fishing trip.

571
00:42:31,465 --> 00:42:34,134
<i>Hey, Soo-hyun. It's me, Moon-jae.</i>

572
00:42:34,218 --> 00:42:35,594
<i>Can you talk for a moment?</i>

573
00:42:36,095 --> 00:42:38,222
I need you to check something for me.

574
00:42:38,722 --> 00:42:40,391
Just in case.

575
00:43:23,934 --> 00:43:24,852
Got a bite.

576
00:49:02,606 --> 00:49:05,525
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
